# Vercel Preview environment variable reference
#
# ⚠️ This file is documentation, not a dotenv file Vercel reads.
# Set every variable below in Vercel → Project → Settings → Environment
# Variables, scoped to "Preview" (or `vercel env add <NAME> preview`).
# Keep Preview values separate from Production — never share buckets,
# databases, or secrets between the two.
#
# Do NOT set APP_URL for Preview: APP_URL resolves from VERCEL_BRANCH_URL
# automatically so each branch keeps a stable URL across pushes.
# scripts/setup-cloud-dev.sh walks through provisioning all of this.

# ── Required ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ParadeDB / PostgreSQL. Must be a remote Postgres with the `vector` and
# `pg_search` extensions (paradedb/paradedb image — a persistent container
# host or VM). Neon is NOT compatible (no pg_search).
# Currently provisioned: dedicated `orvilo-preview-pg` container on the
# existing OCI Always-Free host (see scripts/setup-cloud-dev.sh). The PG
# The endpoint certificate is signed by a private CA. DATABASE_SSL_CA makes
# node-postgres verify both that CA and the database hostname.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://user:password@host:25432/orvilo_preview?sslmode=require&uselibpqcompat=true
DATABASE_DRIVER=node
# Private CA used to verify the Preview PostgreSQL server (literal \n accepted).
DATABASE_SSL_CA=-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\npreview-postgres-ca\n-----END CERTIFICATE-----

# Redis — dedicated TLS-only `orvilo-preview-redis` container alongside
# ParadeDB. REDIS_TLS_CA pins its private CA; use literal \n escapes when an
# environment-variable provider cannot store multiline values.
REDIS_URL=rediss://default:password@host:26380
REDIS_PREFIX=orvilo-preview
AGENT_RUNTIME_REDIS_PREFIX=orvilo-preview
REDIS_TLS=1
REDIS_TLS_CA=-----BEGIN CERTIFICATE-----\npreview-ca\n-----END CERTIFICATE-----

# Cloudflare R2 (S3-compatible). Dedicated preview bucket.
S3_ACCESS_KEY_ID=r2-access-key-id
S3_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=r2-secret-access-key
S3_ENDPOINT=https://account-id.r2.cloudflarestorage.com
S3_BUCKET=orvilo-preview
S3_REGION=auto
S3_SET_ACL=0

# Auth — generate preview-specific values, never reuse production ones.
#   AUTH_SECRET / KEY_VAULTS_SECRET:  openssl rand -base64 32
#   JWKS_KEY:                         node scripts/generate-oidc-jwk.mjs
AUTH_SECRET=preview-only-auth-secret
KEY_VAULTS_SECRET=preview-only-key-vaults-secret
JWKS_KEY={"keys":[...]}

# ── Agent async runtime ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# QStash/Upstash Workflow 正在迁往 Hatchet —— 新部署不需要配；不配时 agent
# 异步步骤退化为同步执行，应用本身照常工作。
# QSTASH_TOKEN=eyJxxx
# QSTASH_CURRENT_SIGNING_KEY=sig_xxx
# QSTASH_NEXT_SIGNING_KEY=sig_yyy

# ── Optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Agent web search. Unset = search tool reports NOT_IMPLEMENTED; the rest of
# the app still works.
# SEARXNG_URL=https://your-searxng.example.com

# Rate-limited dev keys are fine for previews.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-xxx
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-xxx

# ── CI-side secrets (GitHub → Settings → Secrets, not Vercel) ─────────────
# VERCEL_AUTOMATION_BYPASS_SECRET  Vercel → Project → Settings → Deployment
#                                Protection → "Protection Bypass for Automation"
# PREVIEW_DATABASE_URL           same value as the Vercel Preview DATABASE_URL;
#                                the E2E runner routes it through the OCI SSH host
#                                and uses it to seed the test user
# ORACLE_HOST / ORACLE_SSH_KEY   OCI SSH tunnel used by Preview Smoke / E2E
# ORACLE_SSH_KNOWN_HOSTS         pinned known_hosts entries for ORACLE_HOST
# PREVIEW_DB_ADMIN_URL           admin connection for per-PR databases
#                                (preview-db.yml / preview-cleanup.yml)
# PRODUCTION_DATABASE_URL        used by db-migrate.yml (dispatch only)
# VERCEL_TOKEN / VERCEL_ORG_ID / VERCEL_PROJECT_ID
#                                per-PR env provisioning via the Vercel API
# VERCEL_PREVIEW_DEPLOYMENT_GATE  repository variable, default closed; set to
#                                open only after exact-head E2E passes, the
#                                Vercel token preflight is expected to pass,
#                                and the Vercel deployment quota is confirmed.
